   "source": [
    "# PriceCheck — Dataset Exploration\n",
    "**ICS 3202: Artificial Intelligence — Project Deliverable 1**\n",
    "\n",
    "**Group problem area:** A mobile app that lets shoppers in **Nairobi** check whether the price of an item at a supermarket is fair, by comparing it against a model trained on historical price data. The model is powered by an ML price-prediction engine.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Dataset explored:** Kenya. Food Prices, from the World Food Programme (WFP) Price Database, distributed via the Humanitarian Data Exchange (HDX). The dataset was filtered to include data, from Nairobi markets."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1d75e1a3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Candidate open-source datasets\n",
    "\n",
    "| # | Dataset | Description | Expected output variable |\n",
    "|---|---------|-------------|---------------------------|\n",
    "| 1 | **Kenya - Food Prices** (WFP / HDX, [data.humdata.org/dataset/wfp-food-prices-for-kenya](https://data.humdata.org/dataset/wfp-food-prices-for-kenya)) | Monthly price records for staple commodities (maize, rice, beans, sugar, etc.) across ~380 markets in Kenya, from 2006 to present. Directly downloadable CSV, no login required. | `price` (or `usdprice`) — the recorded price of a commodity at a given market and date |\n",
    "| 2 | **Kenya Supermarkets Data** (Kaggle, Emmanuel Kens) | 2017 point-of-sale-style transaction records from Kenyan supermarkets: item, category, unit price, quantity | `unit_price` — the price of a specific item |\n",
    "| 3 | **Kenya: Average Retail Market Prices of Selected Food Crops** (KNBS, via HDX) | Average retail prices of food crops (maize, beans, cabbages, tomatoes, etc.) 2014-2018 | `average_retail_price` |\n",
    "| 4 | **Kenya - Consumer Price Indices (CPI) and Inflation Rates** (KNBS, via HDX) | Monthly CPI and inflation rate by commodity category | `cpi` / `inflation_rate` |\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why the WFP Kenya Food Prices dataset was selected\n",
    "- It is the biggest and most up-to-date of the candidates. It has data, from 2006 to the present and it is updated every month.\n",
    "- The market field has Nairobi in it so we can filter to just Nairobi price observations. That matches our groups scope.\n",
    "- It has a CSV file that can be downloaded directly without any need for login or authentication. This is different, from the Kaggle option which requires API credentials to access the data.\n",
    "- `price` is a continuous output variable. `Price` fits a price‑prediction or price‑check machine‑learning engine well.\n",
    "\n",
    
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e281be23",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Fetching the dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "The CSV file is hosted directly on HDX. Note that the WFP/HDX food-price files contain a **HXL tag row** immediately after the header for example `#date` or `#adm1+name`. We skip that **HXL tag row** when loading the CSV.\n",
    "\n",
    "*If this direct link ever changes, get the latest one from the \"Kenya - Food Prices\" page on [data.humdata.org](https://data.humdata.org/dataset/wfp-food-prices-for-kenya) and swap it into `URL` below.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "3aa644d7",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "URL = \"https://data.humdata.org/dataset/e0d3fba6-f9a2-45d7-b949-140c455197ff/resource/517ee1bf-2437-4f8c-aa1b-cb9925b9d437/download/wfp_food_prices_ken.csv\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# row 0 = column headers, row 1 = HXL hashtags (not real data) -> skip it\n",
    "df_all = pd.read_csv(URL, skiprows=[1])\n",
    "print(\"Columns available:\", list(df_all.columns))\n",
    "df_all.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "beae7d50",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Filtering to Nairobi\n",
    "\n",
    "The full dataset includes markets from, over Kenya.. Our group is focused only on Nairobi. So we narrow it down to the rows where either `admin1` (that’s the county or region) or `market` name shows Nairobi."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "24b279cf",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "nairobi_mask = (\n",
    "    df_all[\"admin1\"].astype(str).str.contains(\"Nairobi\", case=False, na=False)\n",
    "    | df_all[\"market\"].astype(str).str.contains(\"Nairobi\", case=False, na=False)\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "df = df_all[nairobi_mask].reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "print(f\"Nairobi rows: {len(df)} out of {len(df_all)} total rows\")\n",
    "df.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "590fa1e3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Data Exploration\n",
    "\n",
    "### a) How many rows and columns are contained in the dataset?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "2daa3017",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "num_rows, num_cols = df.shape\n",
    "print(f\"Rows: {num_rows}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Columns: {num_cols}\")\n",
    "df.shape"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "54db136b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### b) What datatypes are contained in the dataset?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a648a9ef",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df.dtypes"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "215af79a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### c) Is the dataset complete? i.e. no missing values?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a8aa43f1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "missing = df.isnull().sum()\n",
    "print(missing)\n",
    "print()\n",
    "is_complete = missing.sum() == 0\n",
    "print(f\"Dataset is complete (no missing values): {is_complete}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "if not is_complete:\n",
    "    print()\n",
    "    print(\"Columns with missing values:\")\n",
    "    print(missing[missing > 0])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9f0d94b7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### d) Slice out the first 15 rows and last 20 rows, merge into `df_sample`, and display it"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "86d1eac4",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df_sample = pd.concat([df.head(15), df.tail(20)], ignore_index=True)\n",
    "df_sample"
   ]
  }
 ],
